{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 10,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.971,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.562,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Expressions Using Letter-Numbers"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.108
          ],
          "content": "Recalling how we open brackets in an arithmetic expression, we get"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.113,
            0.728,
            0.132
          ],
          "content": "(40x+75y)-(6x+10y)=(40x+75y)-6x-10y",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.136,
            0.848,
            0.174
          ],
          "content": "Since the terms can be added in any order, the remaining bracket can be opened and the expression becomes $40x+75y+-6x+-10y$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.174,
            0.696,
            0.192
          ],
          "content": "We can group the like terms together, This results in"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.383,
            0.197,
            0.615,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}&40x + - 6x + 75y + - 10y \\\\&= (40 - 6)x + (75 - 10)y \\\\&\\quad\\quad\\quad= 34x + 65y.\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.281,
            0.846,
            0.319
          ],
          "content": "The expression $( 4 0 x + 7 5 y ) - ( 6 x + 1 0 y )$ is simplified to $3 4 x   \\text{+ }   6 5 y _ { \\text{: } }$ which is the total amount paid in rupees."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.327,
            0.621,
            0.368
          ],
          "content": "Could we have written the initial expression as (40x + 75y) + (– 6x – 10y)?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.815,
            0.316,
            0.906,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": "Math Talk"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.387,
            0.848,
            0.463
          ],
          "content": "**Example 8:** Charu has been through three rounds of a quiz. Her scores in the three rounds are $7 p - 3 q ,   8 p - 4 q ,$ and 6p – 2q. Here, p represents the score for a correct answer and q represents the penalty for an incorrect answer."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.478,
            0.548,
            0.501
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "What do each of the expressions mean?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.509,
            0.848,
            0.547
          ],
          "content": "If the score for a correct answer is 4 (p = 4) and the penalty for a wrong answer is 1 (q = 1), find Charu’s score in the first round."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.547,
            0.847,
            0.583
          ],
          "content": "Charu’s score is $7 \\times 4 = 3 \\times 1$ . We can evaluate this expression by writing it as a sum of terms."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.584,
            0.589,
            0.601
          ],
          "content": "7 \\times 4 - 3 \\times 1 = 7 \\times 4 - 3 \\times 1 = 28 + -3 = 25",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.602,
            0.701,
            0.62
          ],
          "content": "What are her scores in the second and third rounds?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.62,
            0.848,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": "What if there is no penalty? What will be the value of q in that situation?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.656,
            0.639,
            0.675
          ],
          "content": "What is her final score after the three rounds?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.676,
            0.846,
            0.713
          ],
          "content": "Her final score will be the sum of the three scores: $( 7 p - 3 q ) + ( 8 p - 4 q ) + ( 6 p - 2 q ) .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.713,
            0.846,
            0.748
          ],
          "content": "Since the terms can be added in any order, we can remove the brackets and write"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.75,
            0.836,
            0.833
          ],
          "content": "7p + – 3q + 8p + – 4q + 6p + –2q = 7p + 8p + 6p + – (3q) + – (4q) + – (2q) (by swapping and grouping) = (7 + 8 + 6)p + – (3 + 4 + 2)q = 21p + – 9q"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.824,
            0.284,
            0.841
          ],
          "content": "= 2 1 p - 9 q .",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.84,
            0.847,
            0.879
          ],
          "content": "Charu’s total score after three rounds is 21p – 9q. Her friend Krishita’s score after three rounds is $2 3 p - 7 q$"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.813,
            0.939,
            0.838,
            0.954
          ],
          "content": "91"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
